Execute malware and threat detection:
1) Run python3 tools/scripts/malware_scanner.py --strict . (or npm run scan:malware).
2) Scan for reverse shell signatures (/dev/tcp, nc -e, pty.spawn), base64 execution pipelines, LD_PRELOAD hijacking, and credential dumping sinks.
3) Verify absence of disguised binary payloads (ELF/PE/Mach-O magic bytes) in text files.
4) Audit external dependencies for supply chain tampering.
Propose atomic defensive mitigations on branch jules/malware-defense-patch via Pull Request. DO NOT attempt direct merge to main."
